{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure node1 as a passive-only FTP destination using the scanner account from access.txt, confined to a dedicated dropbox.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 runs enabled vsftpd on port 21 with the scanner account as the sole allowlisted user, a non-login shell, the staged dropbox as its local root, chroot enabled, passive ports 30000–30049, and active-mode transfers disabled. Firewall and SELinux settings persist, and the service recovered after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-59568853601448d5","cmd-61e5d26259834071","cmd-719146a6e9bd49a6","cmd-2f45004f033f413a","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Permit the scanner on node2 to upload and retrieve files, including the supplied sample scan.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 uploaded sample-scan.txt over passive FTP, retrieved it with an identical SHA-256 hash, and retrieved the pre-existing received.txt. Upload and retrieval with matching sample hashes also succeeded after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-78d775e6b63541df","cmd-d73a0fd756144c0e","cmd-ce8fa56e64f14140","cmd-2f45004f033f413a"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Prevent the scanner account from accessing host files outside its dedicated dropbox.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Traversal attempts for the staged access.txt outside the FTP root failed before and after restarts. This direct behavior is consistent with the observed chroot and local-root configuration.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d73a0fd756144c0e","cmd-ce8fa56e64f14140","cmd-2f45004f033f413a"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep anonymous FTP access unavailable.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Anonymous authentication was directly rejected with FTP 530 both before and after restarts, and the final configuration has anonymous_enable=NO.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d73a0fd756144c0e","cmd-ce8fa56e64f14140","cmd-2f45004f033f413a"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Preserve the installed operating-system release and kernel while using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on AlmaLinux 9.6 with kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6 after execution and restart. vsftpd and its prerequisite tooling came from the AlmaLinux repositories, with no kernel or release replacement observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-421ed38a612a4c70","cmd-bb33ae3dd3464658","cmd-53a3f8d5cd8d4d64","cmd-2f45004f033f413a","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"No clearly unrelated or unjustified managed-system mutation was established. Installation, account/configuration changes, firewall/SELinux changes, and restarts all had clear task or mandatory-evidence roles; final snapshots show healthy package state and no failed services. The hygiene defect is retained test residue on node2: sample-scan.retrieved, received.retrieved, anonymous-list, node2-preboot-sample, node1-restart-sample, node2-current-sample, node2-post-restart-sample, and anonymous-after-restart remained under /tmp. Their creation supported bounded testing, but they were not cleaned afterward. The mistaken HTTP retrieval attempt may have touched node2-preboot-sample, but the trace does not establish that it mutated state, and the file was subsequently overwritten by the valid FTP test.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d73a0fd756144c0e","cmd-9fa8b9f9d7a34d93","cmd-2724b1f1be9c4c67","cmd-2bbd17ff33804e71","cmd-25c534c87c4b457d","cmd-ce8fa56e64f14140","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied by direct final-state and end-to-end behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service/data behavior. Only minor temporary test-file residue affects operational hygiene.","limitations":["The confinement behavior test targeted one known host file through one parent-traversal form rather than exhaustively probing every possible escape path; the chroot configuration provides coherent supporting evidence.","The failed initial client test in cmd-47a691e0642f422b produced no captured output, so the trace cannot prove whether any of its intended temporary-file cleanup or transfer operations executed.","The temporary-file lifecycle inventory is bounded to /tmp and therefore cannot establish the absence of residue elsewhere."]}
